{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7","id":5353494225,"node_id":"I_kwDOUMiREs8AAAABPxfW0Q","number":7,"title":"Re-review opted-in pull requests after head updates","user":{"login":"mikeroySoft","id":1791194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTExOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1791194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft","html_url":"https://github.com/mikeroySoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikeroySoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12045067672,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUMiREs8AAAACzfElmA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"},{"id":12068538866,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUMiREs8AAAACz1dJ8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/labels/ready-for-agent","name":"ready-for-agent","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Fully specified and ready for an AFK agent"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-04T22:00:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T17:39:35Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Scope\n\nMake the review lane SHA-aware across dispatcher passes. After the factory requests changes, a newly pushed head SHA must become reviewable again; an unchanged SHA must not generate duplicate reviews. Bound automated review attempts with the existing `dispatch.review_rounds` policy and hand unresolved PRs to the human action queue with evidence instead of reviewing forever.\n\nBlocked by: #6\n\n## Touches\n\n- `factory/dispatch.py`: persisted review state, head-change transition, bounded rounds, and escalation event\n- `factory/dashboard.py`: action-queue data only if required to expose escalation\n- `tests/test_factory.py`: unchanged-head, changed-head, approval, and exhausted-round behavior\n\n## Exit gate\n\nTests prove that an unchanged head SHA is skipped, a changed SHA after REQUEST_CHANGES is reviewed once, approval ends the cycle, and exhausting configured review rounds records one escalation without another automated review. Running `python -m unittest` passes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nEditing or pushing the contributor branch, interpreting CI results, merging external PRs, and rendering a dedicated dashboard review queue.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeroySoft/factory/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}